  "docsMarkdown": "# Ledger API Reference\n\nAll routes except `/api/auth/*` require `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (see `/api/auth/login`).\n\n## Auth\n\n### POST /api/auth/signup\nCreate a new account. Returns `{ token, account: { id, email, name } }`.\n\n### POST /api/auth/login\nAuthenticate with email/password. Returns `{ token, account: { id, email, name } }`.\n\n## Clients\n\n### GET /api/clients\nList clients for the authenticated account. Returns `{ clients: Client[] }`.\n\n### POST /api/clients\nCreate a client. Returns `{ client: Client }`.\n\n### GET /api/clients/:id\nFetch a client by id. Returns `{ client: Client }`.\n\nA `Client` has: `id, accountId, name, email, phone, billingType, recurringStatus, createdAt`.\n\n## Invoices\n\n### GET /api/invoices\nList invoices for the authenticated account. Returns `{ invoices: InvoiceSummary[] }`, where each summary includes `id, invoiceNumber, status, currency, totalCents, issueDate, dueDate, customer_name`.\n\n### POST /api/invoices\nCreate an invoice with line items for a client. Returns `{ invoice: Invoice }`.\n\n### GET /api/invoices/:id\nFetch a single invoice. Customer fields are nested under a `customer` object as `customer.id`, `customer.profile.name`, `customer.profile.email`, `customer.subscription.status` (previously flattened onto the response as `customer_name`, `customer_email`, `subscription_status`). Supports `?displayCurrency=XXX` to add converted `displayCurrency` / `displayTotalCents` fields alongside the original `currency` / `totalCents`. Also returns `lineItems: LineItem[]`.\n\n### POST /api/invoices/:id/send\nMark an invoice as `sent`. Returns `{ invoice: Invoice }`.\n\nAn `Invoice` has: `id, accountId, clientId, invoiceNumber, status, currency, subtotalCents, taxCents, totalCents, issueDate, dueDate, createdAt`.\n\nA `LineItem` has: `id, invoiceId, description, quantity, unitPriceCents, amountCents`.\n"
